# A terminal's readers in the process table's late entries (roadmap
# memory.md M1): init starts tests/posix/late.c (TEST_POSIX_LATE), which
# holds children until the next process takes entry 16, then entry 22, and
# has it read a line each time. The server kept the readers as a 16-bit
# mask, a bit an entry: a reader past entry 15 had no bit, was never woken,
# and the test's typing never came (E6, E8). Then the table's last entry,
# which the root's slots kept out of reach until M4 (E8). At the end it
# reads again, so that the test ends.
program: none
define: TEST_POSIX_LATE
keys: ab\ncde\nfghi\n
match: contains
timeout: 120
---
late: the reader at entry 16 read 3 bytes
late: the reader at entry 22 read 4 bytes
late: the reader at the table's last entry read 5 bytes
late: done
